; form-choice-flow-live.fk — the choices process: every real decision this
; body makes gives itself into the glass.
; preflight-exec: forbidden
;
; One kernel, no forks, no scans, no files: every second it reads the live
; page ledgers of its own kernel (crystallize or walk, box or fold, reuse or
; mint), takes the organs and resource-governor frames that already stand in
; the live telemetry space, walks the roster the glass itself walks, and gives
; ONE snapshot into the `choices` frame — every choice point with its flow,
; its restriction and its holding, every gap and wound with what it asks for,
; and the play of the whole sequence scored by its narrowest gate.
;
; It counts nothing the body was not already counting. The one ledger that
; grows here is the governor's admission, and it grows through the body's own
; three outcomes, one a tick.
;
; The glass reads that frame like any other publisher, beside the organs frame.
; The logic lives in form/form-stdlib/form-choice-flow-glass.bml and
; form/form-stdlib/form-choice-flow-sources.bml; this file is the carrier.
;
; preludes: form/form-stdlib/hearth.bml form/form-stdlib/form-choice-flow-glass.bml

(fcfg-loop (hearth-telemetry-root) (fcfg-state-empty))
